PriorityQueue is a heap-based queue:

Elements are not stored or retrieved in insertion order

The element with the highest priority (by natural order or a custom Comparator) is always at the head

add() and poll() are O(log n); peek() is O(1)

Duplicates are allowed (unlike Sets)

Backed by a binary heap (min-heap by default)

⚠️ Important: Iterating a PriorityQueue with a for-each loop does NOT give sorted order — it gives heap-array order. To get sorted output, you must poll() repeatedly
